    "q-141639": {
      "dom_id": "step-q141639",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given the graph of $y=f(x),$ we apply the following transformations in the order given:\n\n1\\. Translate it down by $2$ units\n\n2\\. Translate it to the right by $1$ unit\n\n3\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n\nWhat is the final function expression after applying all the transformations?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the expression, let's apply each of the transformations in turn.\n\n1\\. Translating the graph of $y=f(x)$ down by $2$ units is equivalent to subtracting $2$ from the function expression. Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=f(x)-2.\n  $$\n\n2\\. Translating the graph of $y=f(x)-2$ by $1$ unit to the right is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $(x-1).$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=f(x-1)-2.\n  $$\n\n3\\. Stretching the graph of $y=f(x-1)-2$ by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $y$-axis is equivalent to multiplying the function expression by $5.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=5(f(x-1)-2)=5f(x-1)-10.\n  $$\n\nTherefore, the final function expression is  $y=5f(x-1)-10.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
