    "q-142249": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142249",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given the graph of $y=f(x),$ we apply the following transformations in the order given:\n\n1\\. Translate it up by $7$ units\n\n2\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n\n3\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\nWhat is the final function expression after applying all the transformations?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the expression, let's apply each of the transformations in turn.\n\n1\\. Translating the graph of $y=f(x)$ up by $7$ units is equivalent to adding $7$ to $f(x).$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=f(x)+7.\n  $$\n\n2\\. Stretching the graph of $y=f(x)+7$ by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis is equivalent to multiplying the function expression by $3.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=3(f(x)+7)=3f(x)+21.\n  $$\n\n3\\. Stretching the graph of $y=3f(x)+21$ by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $x$-axis is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $\\frac{x}{2}.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=3f(\\frac{x}{2})+21.\n  $$\n\nTherefore, the final function expression is $y=3f(\\frac{x}{2})+21.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
