    "q-141735": {
      "dom_id": "step-q141735",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given the graph of $y=f(x),$ we apply the following transformations in the order given:\n\n1\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n\n2\\. Translate it to the left by $4$ units\n\n3\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{7}$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\nWhat is the final function expression after applying all the transformations?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the expression, let's apply each of the transformations in turn.\n\n1\\. Stretching the graph of $y=f(x)$ by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis is equivalent to multiplying the function expression by $3.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=3f(x).\n  $$\n\n2\\. Translating the graph of $y=3f(x)$ by $4$ units to the left is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $(x+4).$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=3f(x+4).\n  $$\n\n3\\. Stretching the graph of $y=3f(x+4)$ by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{7}$ parallel to the $x$-axis is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $7x.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=3f((7x)+4)=3f(7x+4).\n  $$\n\nTherefore, the final function expression is $y=3f(7x+4).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
