    "q-142251": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142251",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Given the graph of $y=f(x),$ we apply the following transformations in the order given:\n\n1\\. Translate it to the right by $1$ unit\n\n2\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{5}$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\n3\\. Translate it up by $3$ units\n\nWhat is the final function expression after applying all the transformations?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the expression, let's apply each of the transformations in turn.\n\n1\\. Translating the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $1$ unit to the right is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ by $(x-1).$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=f(x-1).\n  $$\n\n2\\. Stretching the graph of $y=f(x-1)$ by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{5}$ parallel to the $x$-axis is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $5x.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=f((5x)-1))=f(5x-1).\n  $$\n\n3\\. Translating the graph of $y=f(5x-1)$ up by $3$ units is equivalent to adding $3$ to the function expression. Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=f(5x-1)+3.\n  $$\n\nTherefore, the final function expression is $y=f(5x-1)+3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
