    "q-141747": {
      "dom_id": "step-q141747",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given the graph of $y=f(x),$ we apply the following transformations in the order given:\n\n1\\. Translate it up by $10$ units\n\n2\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{8}$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\n3\\. Translate it to the right by $1$ unit\n\nWhat is the final function expression after applying all the transformations?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the expression, let's apply each of the transformations in turn.\n\n1\\. Translating the graph of $y=f(x)$ up by $10$ units is equivalent to adding $10$ to $f(x).$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=f(x)+10.\n  $$\n\n2\\. Stretching the graph of $y=f(x)+10$ by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{8}$ parallel to the $x$-axis is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $8x.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=f(8x)+10.\n  $$\n\n3\\. Translating the graph of $y=f(8x)+10$ by $1$ unit to the right is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ by $(x-1).$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=f(8(x-1))+10=f(8x-8)+10.\n  $$\n\nTherefore, the final function expression is $y=f(8x-8)+10.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
